T016 evidence: the running system and the bootloader agree on the boot-selection
state. Extracted from a serial capture on 2026-10-28, image built from the tree at
commit 87667f1. Full boot logs are long and repetitive; these are the lines that
carry the result.

--- first boot, at the U-Boot prompt: the seeded region is read ------------------

=> printenv
BOOT_A_LEFT=3
BOOT_B_LEFT=3
BOOT_ORDER=A B
bootcmd=run ota_select
bootdelay=1
[...]
Environment size: 1528/131067 bytes

--- booting: one attempt is spent, written and saved -----------------------------

=> boot
Saving Environment to MMC... Writing to redundant MMC(0)... OK
OTA: booting slot A, 2 attempts left
7649392 bytes read in 491 ms (14.9 MiB/s)
70396 bytes read in 7 ms (9.6 MiB/s)

[    0.000000] Kernel command line: console=ttyS0,115200n8 root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 ro rootfstype=ext4 rootwait
[    2.656221]  mmcblk0: p1 p2 p3 p4
[    2.775027] VFS: Mounted root (ext4 filesystem) readonly on device 179:2.

--- in Linux: fw_printenv reads exactly what U-Boot wrote ------------------------

# fw_printenv
BOOT_A_LEFT=2
BOOT_B_LEFT=3
BOOT_ORDER=A B
ota_left=2
ota_part=2
ota_slot=A
[...]

--- after a reboot: the state persists and the counter walks down ----------------

Loading Environment from MMC... Reading from MMC(0)... OK
Hit any key to stop autoboot: 0
Saving Environment to MMC... Writing to redundant MMC(0)... OK
OTA: booting slot A, 1 attempts left

# fw_printenv BOOT_A_LEFT
BOOT_A_LEFT=1

--- what this proves, and what it does not --------------------------------------

Proven: U-Boot reads the seeded region rather than falling back to its compiled-in
default; setexpr and saveenv work; the counter decrements and survives a reboot; and
fw_printenv in Linux reads the same bytes U-Boot wrote, so /etc/fw_env.config names
the right device, offsets and size.

Not proven by this capture: the write direction. `fw_setenv BOOT_A_LEFT 2` was run
while the value was already 2, so a write that silently went elsewhere would look
identical. Closing it takes one command: set the counter to 3 from Linux, reboot, and
confirm U-Boot announces two attempts left.

--- three other things this capture settles --------------------------------------

1. The clock starts in the past. `omap_rtc 44e3e000.rtc: setting system clock to
   2000-01-01T00:00:00 UTC` -- this board has no RTC backup, so a certificate whose
   validity window opens at build time is not yet valid when a device boots. That
   decides a research item for the staging/production signing work, and it is a real
   behaviour rather than a theoretical worry.

2. The watchdog still does not arm. U-Boot reports `WDT: Started wdt@44e35000 with
   servicing every 1000ms (60s timeout)` and the kernel registers
   `omap_wdt: OMAP Watchdog Timer Rev 0x01: initial timeout 60 sec`, yet the board sat
   at an idle shell for 253 seconds with no userspace watchdog client and was never
   reset. CONFIG_WATCHDOG_OPEN_TIMEOUT=60 was necessary but is not sufficient, so
   FR-032 is not yet satisfied and T034 would fail today.

3. The root filesystem is still remounted read-write: `EXT4-fs (mmcblk0p2):
   re-mounted ... r/w.` at 2.96 s. That is T023, still to do, and this line is the
   check for it.

--- addendum, 2026-10-28: the write direction is now proven ----------------------

The gap named above is closed by t024-us1-second-capture.log. `rauc status mark-good`
set BOOT_A_LEFT to 3 from Linux, and after a power cycle U-Boot announced
"OTA: booting slot A, 2 attempts left", i.e. it read 3 and spent one attempt. The
environment is shared in both directions.
